Berg does, indeed, relate to electromyography (EMG) for exercise tracking. See Berg, atparagraph 1SVG
{EMBED HERE}
0.1370.03710003]. More particularly, Berg relates to "monitoring biometric signals of a usercomprising: a garment", "a set of biometric sensors" and "a portable control module". See Berg, claim 1. Berg provides a very general description of EMG and expressly shows (see FIG. 3B) positioning of sensors on an upper torso location of a t-shirt.
